    "answer": {
      "short": "One symbol represents 4 pies. Monday: 3 symbols; Tuesday: 5; Wednesday: 2; Thursday: 4; Friday: 6.",
      "worked": "Use one symbol for 4 pies.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Monday symbols}&=12\\div4=3\\\\\\text{Tuesday symbols}&=20\\div4=5\\\\\\text{Wednesday symbols}&=8\\div4=2\\\\\\text{Thursday symbols}&=16\\div4=4\\\\\\text{Friday symbols}&=24\\div4=6\\end{align*}$$\nDraw equal-sized, equally spaced symbols in aligned rows and include the key.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
        {
          "id": "v2-p9-practice-slot-7-2-slot-7-solution-pictogram",
          "role": "solution",
          "format": "tikz",
          "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"slot-7 pictogram solution\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm,line width=0.5pt,text=black,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,every node/.style={inner sep=0pt}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\def\\pie{\\draw (0,0) circle (2.3);\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (0,0)--(0,2.3);\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (0,0)--(2,-1.15);\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (0,0)--(-2,-1.15);}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (0,9) rectangle (78,-52);\n\\node[anchor=west] at (0,5) {Key:};\n\\begin{scope}[shift={(12,5)},scale=.7]\\pie\\end{scope}\n\\node[anchor=west] at (15,5) {$=4$ pies};\n\\draw (25,0)--(78,0)--(78,-52)--(0,-52)--(0,-12)--(25,-12)--cycle;\n\\draw (25,-12)--(25,-52) (39,0)--(39,-52);\n\\node[align=center] at (32,-6) {\\textbf{Pies}\\\\\\textbf{sold}};\n\\foreach \\y in {-12,-20,-28,-36,-44}{\\draw (0,\\y)--(78,\\y);}\n\\foreach \\name/\\count/\\row in {Monday/3/1,Tuesday/5/2,Wednesday/2/3,Thursday/4/4,Friday/6/5}{\n\\node[anchor=center] at (12.5,{-8*\\row-8}) {\\textbf{\\name}};\n\\node at (32,{-8*\\row-8}) {\\pgfmathparse{int(4*\\count)}\\pgfmathresult};\n\\foreach \\j in {1,...,\\count}{\\begin{scope}[shift={({42+4.2*(\\j-1)},{-8*\\row-8})},scale=.7]\\pie\\end{scope}}\n}\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
